{"type":"message","id":"2b230b37","parentId":"7d343dc6","timestamp":"2026-04-13T11:49:41.936Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_Imw9g8AjqH4bSFGcBXpQkLKY|fc_03c2dba4808dc8ae0169dcd855ac5c8191b6279d0bfc96c8d0","toolName":"edit","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully replaced text in /home/node/.openclaw/workspace-demo-agent/TOOLS.md."}],"details":{"diff":"    ...\n 28 - **Limits:** This is still a prototype pipeline output, not a diagnosis. The X-AI component may be integrated in the workflow even when its own returned tracking data is limited.\n 29 - **Output structure:** \"Kidney Cancer Detector\", \"Image Analyzer\", \"xAI\", \"Result Interpretation\", \"Recommendended next steps\" (at the end of the \"Image Analyzer\" section, leave a brief statament mentioning that the heatmap image is attached). \n 30 - **Final message:** Always remember to the use that the tool output as a preliminary signal, not as an actual diagnosis.\n 31 \n-32 ## llm_distillator\n+32 ## distillation-tool\n 33 - **Role:** Distill the outputs of one or more diagnostic tools together with the symptom discussion and immediate conversation context into a clear patient-facing summary.\n 34 - **Use for:** after symptoms have already been discussed and a diagnostic tool has just run, especially when its output needs to be translated into a coherent explanation for the user.\n 35 - **Suggestion rule:** Suggest this skill only once there has been enough symptom discussion to frame the case and a tool has just produced a diagnostic result or preliminary diagnosis.\n 36 - **Presentation rule:** Use it to convert raw or fragmented tool output into a concise explanation that matches the agent’s diagnostic output structure and preserves the distinction between tool findings and clinical interpretation.\n    ...","firstChangedLine":32},"isError":false,"timestamp":1776080981935}}
